Privacy Policy — Hopwise: Frog Escape Puzzle
Last updated: November 14, 2026

HyperXcite Studio ("we", "us") makes the mobile game Hopwise: Frog Escape Puzzle (the "Game"). This policy explains what information is collected when you play the Game and how it is used.

1. Information we collect
We do not ask for your name, email address, phone number, or any account. The Game can be played without signing in.

Game progress stored on your device. Your levels, stars, coins, frog skins, settings and purchases are saved only on your device. We do not receive this data. It is deleted when you uninstall the Game.

Information collected by our partners. The Game uses third-party services that may collect information automatically:

Service	Purpose	Information it may collect
Google AdMob	Showing ads (rewarded videos and ads between levels)	Advertising ID, IP address, device model, operating system, language, approximate location (from IP), ad interactions
Google User Messaging Platform	Asking for consent to personalized ads where required by law (e.g. EEA, UK, Switzerland)	Your consent choice, device information
Google Play Billing	Processing in-app purchases	Purchase details. Payments are handled entirely by Google; we never see your card or payment information
These services follow their own privacy policies:

Google Privacy Policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy
How Google uses information from apps that use its services: https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites
AdMob and ads: https://support.google.com/admob/answer/6128543
2. How the information is used
To show ads, including personalized ads if you allow them
To limit how often ads appear and to measure their performance
To deliver and restore in-app purchases (coins, frog bundle, Remove Ads)
To keep the Game working and fix problems
We do not sell your personal information.

3. Your choices
Ad consent: If you are in a region where consent is required, the Game asks before showing personalized ads. You can change your choice at any time in Settings → Privacy choices in the Game.
Advertising ID: On Android you can reset or delete your advertising ID in your device settings (Settings → Privacy → Ads).
Remove Ads: You can buy "Remove Ads" to stop the ads between levels. Optional rewarded videos remain available.
Delete your data: Uninstalling the Game deletes all game data stored on your device. To ask about data held by Google, see the Google links above.
4. Children
The Game is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal information through the Game, contact us and we will help remove it.

5. Data security
Game data stays on your device. Information sent to our partners is transmitted using encryption (HTTPS).

6. Changes to this policy
We may update this policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with a new "Last updated" date.

